=== Sanity check with (X_0, Y_0) = (0, 0) (2-torsion) ===

Clean factorization of pi_2 fiber:
  F|_{X=X_0,Y=Y_0} = 4*alpha*m^2*n^2 - beta*(m^2-n^2)^2
  where alpha = Y_0^2 - X_0^2(X_0+1), beta = X_0(X_0+1).

Note: alpha/beta = (Y_0^2 - X_0^2(X_0+1)) / (X_0(X_0+1))
    = Y_0^2/(X_0(X_0+1)) - X_0
    = Y_0^2/(X_0(X_0+1)) - X_0

On E_PCP: Y^2 = X(X+1)(X+q^2), so Y_0^2 = X_0(X_0+1)(X_0+q^2).
=> Y_0^2 / (X_0(X_0+1)) = X_0 + q^2.
=> alpha/beta = (X_0 + q^2) - X_0 = q^2.

**KEY: alpha/beta = q^2 for any point (X_0,Y_0) on E_PCP(q)!**

Verify with X_0 = 1, q^2 = 400/441
  alpha/beta = 400/441
  q^2 = 400/441
  Match: 1

=== KEY GEOMETRIC INSIGHT ===

For (X_0, Y_0) on E_PCP(q), the pi_2 fiber is:
  (m^2-n^2)^2 = 4 q^2 m^2 n^2
  <=> m^2 - n^2 = ±2 q m n
  <=> q = ±(m^2-n^2)/(2mn).

This is just the Pythagorean conic { (m,n) : q(m,n) = ±q }.

Geometric structure of W:
  W = { (X, Y, m, n) : (X,Y) in E_PCP(q(m,n)) }
  pi_2 fiber over (X_0,Y_0) = preimage of q^2 = q(X_0,Y_0)^2 under q-map.

Equivalently, W is a fiber product:
  W = E_total ×_{q-line} Pyth_total
where:
  E_total -> A^1_q is the elliptic fibration with fiber E_PCP(q)
  Pyth_total -> A^1_q is the Pythagorean conic fibration (m,n) -> q(m,n)

Both are 2-folds. W is a 3-fold (fiber product of 2 fibrations of dim 2 over dim 1).

=== Birational type: W is uniruled ===

The pi_2 fibers are conics — rational curves.
Through every point of W there passes a rational curve.
=> W is uniruled, Kodaira dimension κ(W) = -∞.

Equivalently: W is birational to E_q × P^1 — a P^1-bundle over the elliptic surface E_q.
More precisely:
  W is birational to the elliptic surface S := { (X,Y,q) : E_PCP(q) }
  product with P^1 (the Pythagorean conic parametrized by t=m/n).

=== Mordell-Weil / Lang implications ===

Faltings 1991: needs subvariety of abelian variety.
  W is UNIRULED => Albanese(W) = 0 => Faltings 1991 INAPPLICABLE.

Lang conjecture (general type): not applicable since κ(W) = -∞.

Bombieri-Lang for uniruled: rational points are Zariski-dense in general.
  Specifically: rational points cover the entire surface S_pyth × E
  for any rank-positive q.

=> The 3-fold lift W does NOT give PCP closure.
=> No new global finiteness from this direction.

=== Why this is NOT a setback ===

The pi_2 fibration reveals a deep structural fact:
the (m,n) parameters and the (X,Y) coordinates are INDEPENDENT directions.
Fixing (X_0,Y_0) gives only the Pythagorean conic constraint on (m,n).

This was already implicit in the existing framework:
the closure relies on PER-FIBER analysis (Silverman+Ingram-Mahe)
plus rank-jump locus density 0, NOT on global 3-fold finiteness.

The 3-fold W does NOT add new control; it just packages the existing structure.
